title: '[pallet-revive] Serve the ETH RPC from inside the node'

doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    A `polkadot-omni-node` built with the new `experimental-eth-rpc-in-node` compile-time
    feature serves the Ethereum JSON-RPC server itself on `--eth-rpc-port` (8545 by
    default), instead of running a separate `eth-rpc` process over a loopback WebSocket.
    Experimental: the in-process transport between the embedded server and the node (how
    it dispatches JSON-RPC calls into the node without a socket) is still being reworked
    and may change.

- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-revive-eth-rpc` gains `in_process::InProcessRpcClient`, a `subxt` `RpcClientT`
    that dispatches into a node's in-memory `RpcModule` instead of a socket, and
    `service::start_embedded`, which builds the ETH RPC client on it and spawns the
    server on an existing `TaskManager`. Both are gated behind the crate's own
    `experimental-eth-rpc-in-node` feature, off by default, which `polkadot-omni-node-lib`
    forwards under the same feature name.

    `polkadot-omni-node-lib` now optionally depends on `pallet-revive-eth-rpc`, which
    build-depends on `revive-dev-runtime` for its subxt metadata. That's cyclic through
    the umbrella crate (which re-exports `polkadot-omni-node-lib`), so `revive-dev-runtime`
    now depends on individual `polkadot-sdk` crates instead of the umbrella one, and gains
    `try-runtime`/`runtime-benchmarks` features so it still builds with `--all-features`.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node
  bump: patch
- name: revive-dev-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: revive-dev-node
  bump: patch
